ve a  record call user it has three fields  named favorite number favorite color  it's a record type scheme as the user  typically an Avro is it uses a write the  header to the top of the file and in  this file you have these or datum blocks  which are the records and you could have  a billion or a million of these and the  schema has very little overhead like  0.001 percent on average but what  happens if you send this over the wire  now all of a sudden you're sending one  data in near real-time but the overhead  of the schema is 99  that is way too much so a trip that we  did a LinkedIn and the casco users and  confluent uses is that you don't send  the schema over the wire what you do is  you store it in a registry somewhere you  get an ID out and you just send the ID  like a single number  it's a across wire so we built and we're  going to open source the schema registry  that's based on the lambda and  essentially the producer will get an ID  but when it registers a schema it'll  send the ID with the data the consumer  will read that it'll deserialize it I  mean it will basically get the schema by  ID cache it and then decode the avro and  all of our pipelines save about 99%  throughput and and that's how we get  like quite a high speed in our pipelines  and our schema registry if you remember  this picture is like deployed wherever  we have Kinesis so I think at this point  I'm actually done with the talk  it was probably kind of fast lots of  details if you have further questions  please come and chat with me later  and I'd like to thank my whole team  which is everybody on this slide and  that's it thank you very much

